---
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <title>Rating Guide & Glossary | Cherie Reads</title>
    <script defer src="/_vercel/insights/script.js"></script>
    <style>
      :root {
        --card-bg: #fcfbf9;
        --border-color: #c4d6c7;
        --text-color: #2c352d;
        --text-muted: #556358;
        --accent: #1e3d24;
        --accent-hover: #122617;
        --hero-bg: #f5f0e6;
        --hero-border: #d8cebc;
        --gold-accent: #8c6d33;
        --gold-bg: #fbf6ec;
        --gold-border: #e6dcc5;
        --sage-accent: #4a6b52;
        --sage-bg: #edf3ee;
        --sage-border: #d3e2d5;
        --serif-font: "Georgia", "Times New Roman", serif;
      }
      body {
        font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif;
        margin: 0;
        padding: 0;
        background: linear-gradient(135deg, #d8e4da 0%, #eef3ef 50%, #d2e0d4 100%);
        color: var(--text-color);
        line-height: 1.6;
        min-height: 100vh;
      }
      header {
        background: rgba(252, 251, 249, 0.95);
        backdrop-filter: blur(8px);
        border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-color);
        padding: 20px 40px;
        display: flex;
        justify-content: space-between;
        align-items: center;
        box-shadow: 0 1px 3px rgba(30, 61, 36, 0.05);
      }
      .brand-container {
        display: flex;
        align-items: center;
        gap: 12px;
        text-decoration: none;
      }
      .brand-icon {
        width: 22px;
        height: 22px;
        object-fit: contain;
      }
      header h1 {
        margin: 0;
        font-family: var(--serif-font);
        font-size: 2rem;
        color: var(--accent);
        letter-spacing: -0.5px;
        font-weight: normal;
        font-style: italic;
      }
      nav a {
        color: var(--text-muted);
        text-decoration: none;
        margin-left: 20px;
        font-weight: 500;
        font-size: 0.95rem;
        transition: color 0.2s;
      }
      nav a:hover, nav a.active {
        color: var(--accent);
      }
      .container {
        max-width: 900px;
        margin: 40px auto;
        padding: 0 20px;
      }
      .content-card {
        background: var(--card-bg);
        border: 1px solid var(--border-color);
        border-radius: 8px;
        padding: 40px;
        box-shadow: 0 4px 16px rgba(30, 61, 36, 0.05);
        margin-bottom: 30px;
      }
      .content-card h2 {
        font-family: var(--serif-font);
        font-size: 1.8rem;
        color: var(--accent);
        margin-top: 0;
        margin-bottom: 15px;
        border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-color);
        padding-bottom: 10px;
      }
      .content-card h3 {
        font-family: var(--serif-font);
        font-size: 1.3rem;
        color: var(--accent);
        margin-top: 25px;
        margin-bottom: 10px;
      }
      .content-card p {
        margin-bottom: 1.2em;
        font-size: 1.02rem;
      }
      .rating-list {
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
        gap: 16px;
        margin-top: 20px;
      }
      .rating-item {
        background: #fdfcfb;
        border: 1px solid var(--border-color);
        border-left: 4px solid var(--gold-accent);
        padding: 16px 20px;
        border-radius: 6px;
      }
      .rating-item strong {
        font-family: var(--serif-font);
        font-size: 1.1rem;
        color: var(--accent);
      }
      .glossary-grid {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
        gap: 20px;
        margin-top: 15px;
      }
      .glossary-item {
        background: #fdfcfb;
        border: 1px solid var(--border-color);
        padding: 14px 16px;
        border-radius: 6px;
      }
      .glossary-item strong {
        color: var(--sage-accent);
        display: block;
        margin-bottom: 4px;
        font-size: 1rem;
      }
      .glossary-item span {
        font-size: 0.9rem;
        color: var(--text-muted);
      }
      @media (max-width: 768px) {
        .glossary-grid {
          grid-template-columns: 1fr;
        }
        .content-card {
          padding: 24px;
        }
      }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <header>
      <a href="/" class="brand-container">
        <img src="/leaf-svgrepo-com.svg" alt="Leaf Icon" class="brand-icon" />
        <h1>Cherie Reads</h1>
      </a>
      <nav>
        <a href="/">Home</a>
        <a href="/guide" class="active">Guide</a>
        <a href="/about">About</a>
      </nav>
    </header>

    <div class="container">
      <!-- Rating System Card -->
      <div class="content-card">
        <h2>Rating Philosophy & System</h2>
        <p>Curious about how I grade my reads? Here is a breakdown of what my star ratings mean:</p>
        
        <div class="rating-list">
          <div class="rating-item">
            <strong>★★★★★ 5 Stars: Exceptional</strong>
            <p>Highly recommended. This book left a lasting impression and will stay with me for a long time.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="rating-item">
            <strong>★★★★☆ 4 Stars: Very Good</strong>
            <p>Highly enjoyable and well-written. A wonderful read that I would gladly recommend to others.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="rating-item">
            <strong>★★★☆☆ 3 Stars: Average</strong>
            <p>An overall decent experience, though not especially memorable, or held back by specific issues like plot holes, weak pacing, or awkward writing.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="rating-item">
            <strong>★★☆☆☆ 2 Stars: Poor</strong>
            <p>There were numerous elements I disliked, and it is not a book I would recommend.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="rating-item" style="border-left-color: #9b1c1c;">
            <strong>★☆☆☆☆ 1 Star / DNF: Abandoned</strong>
            <p>Life is too short for bad books. This is reserved for reads so unengaging or poorly executed that I chose to DNF (Did Not Finish) rather than waste my time.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Glossary Card -->
      <div class="content-card">
        <h2>Book Property Glossary</h2>
        <p>To help you navigate my reviews and find your next great read, I track several specific elements for each book. Hovering over tags on individual review pages will show these definitions, but you can reference the full index here:</p>

        <h3>Pace</h3>
        <div class="glossary-grid">
          <div class="glossary-item"><strong>Slow Burn</strong><span>Deliberate pacing that gradually builds characters, world, or plot.</span></div>
          <div class="glossary-item"><strong>Steady</strong><span>Consistent pacing with a balance between quieter and faster moments.</span></div>
          <div class="glossary-item"><strong>Page Turner</strong><span>Difficult to put down because of suspense, action, or constant momentum.</span></div>
        </div>

        <h3>Brainpower</h3>
        <div class="glossary-grid">
          <div class="glossary-item"><strong>Easy</strong><span>Accessible and straightforward.</span></div>
          <div class="glossary-item"><strong>Moderate</strong><span>Requires some attention but remains easy to follow.</span></div>
          <div class="glossary-item"><strong>Challenging</strong><span>Dense, layered, philosophical, or structurally complex.</span></div>
        </div>

        <h3>Story Focus</h3>
        <div class="glossary-grid">
          <div class="glossary-item"><strong>Character Driven</strong><span>Relationships, growth, and personal journeys are the primary focus.</span></div>
          <div class="glossary-item"><strong>Plot Driven</strong><span>Events, action, or solving problems drive the story.</span></div>
          <div class="glossary-item"><strong>Balanced</strong><span>Characters and plot receive roughly equal attention.</span></div>
        </div>

        <h3>Stakes</h3>
        <div class="glossary-grid">
          <div class="glossary-item"><strong>Low</strong><span>Consequences are mostly personal.</span></div>
          <div class="glossary-item"><strong>Medium</strong><span>Consequences affect families, communities, or smaller groups.</span></div>
          <div class="glossary-item"><strong>High</strong><span>Failure affects kingdoms, civilizations, or the world.</span></div>
        </div>

        <h3>Worldbuilding</h3>
        <div class="glossary-grid">
          <div class="glossary-item"><strong>Light</strong><span>The setting is easy to understand with little explanation.</span></div>
          <div class="glossary-item"><strong>Moderate</strong><span>The world has unique elements but remains accessible.</span></div>
          <div class="glossary-item"><strong>Dense</strong><span>Complex history, cultures, politics, or magic require sustained attention.</span></div>
        </div>

        <h3>Length Feel</h3>
        <div class="glossary-grid">
          <div class="glossary-item"><strong>Short</strong><span>Feels like a quick read.</span></div>
          <div class="glossary-item"><strong>Medium</strong><span>Feels like an average reading commitment.</span></div>
          <div class="glossary-item"><strong>Long</strong><span>Feels like a significant investment of time.</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </body>
</html>
